 want a structured pause for thought, meditation, prayer, or reflection.","short_summary":"An outdoor contemplative path built for walking, stillness, and focused thought.","evidence_claim":"Furman identifies the chapel lawn’s brick labyrinth as a meditative tool and documents people walking, sitting, meditating, praying, and seeking guidance there.","source_url":"https://www.furman.edu/spiritual-life/daniel-chapel/labyrinth/","source_title":"Labyrinth | Office of Spiritual Life | Furman University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://campusmap.furman.edu/","access_notes":"The university describes the outdoor labyrinth as open all day, every day; use it respectfully and yield to organized activities.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"furman-place-of-peace","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Place of Peace","title":"Slow Down at the Lake’s Japanese Temple","subtitle":"Contemplative space beside the Asia Garden","notes":"Walk the adjoining garden or pause for reflection; visit during docent hours when you want historical context about the temple.","short_summary":"A reconstructed Japanese temple and garden setting used for reflection, teaching, and connection.","evidence_claim":"Furman invites visitors to stroll and meditate at the Place of Peace and adjoining Asia Garden; Asian Studies also uses the temple as a teaching tool and meeting space.","source_url":"https://www.furman.edu/place-peace/","source_title":"Place of Peace | Furman University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://campusmap.furman.edu/","access_notes":"Public docents are listed Saturday and Sunday from 1–3 p.m.; outdoor garden access and temple entry may differ, so follow posted signs.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"wa